estuary, Saint-Estèphe is separated from its famous neighbor, Pauillac, only by a stream, yet there are significant differences between them. With 1,229 hectares (3036 acres) it accounts for 8 percent of the vineyard area of the Médoc. Because Saint-Estèphe is marginally further from the gravel-bearing waters of the Garonne river, the soil here is far less stony than that found in the southern part of Haut-Médoc. Instead, a heavy clay and limestone base dominates this area, resulting in poorer-draining soils, delayed ripening and higher acidity levels in the wines.", "grape_text": "Cabernet Franc – Cabernet Sauvignon are two of the key grape varieties (along with Merlot) used in the red wines of Bordeaux. The combined blend of the two has been so successful that it has been adopted in wine regions the world over. Typically Cabernet Sauvignon is the dominant member in this blend, and provides both structure (acidic and tannic) and aromatic complexity (cassis, cedar, tobacco). The Cabernet Franc component brings a lifted, slightly more floral aroma, and a hint of spice on the palate. Exceptions to this rule of Cabernet Sauvignon dominance are most likely to be found in the Loire Valley, where Cabernet Franc has long been a staple red wine variety. In Tuscany this blend has been warmly adopted. Sassicaia – one of Italy''s most famous wines – is arguably one of the world''s finest examples of this marriage of the two Cabernet grapes, and is largely responsible for the proliferation of the style throughout the region. This \"Super Tuscan\" wine is routinely described as having characteristics of cassis and five-spice with firm tannins in its youth. With age these wines soften and start to show more secondary qualities – often led by Cabernet Franc – of tobacco, coffee and earthy minerals.", "critical_acclaim": [{"score": "96", "critic": "Vinous", "context": "2022 vintage", "quote": "Once again, the most elegant wine in Saint-Estèphe."}, {"score": "95", "critic": "Decanter", "context": "2022 vintage", "quote": "An exceptional wine in 2022."}, {"score": "95", "critic": "Jeb Dunnuck", "context": "2022 vintage", "quote": "A seriously good, concentrated, powerful expression."}, {"score": "94", "critic": "James Suckling", "context": "2022 vintage", "quote": "Dark chocolate, cigar box, blackcurrants, white pepper and graphite."}, {"score": "94", "critic": "Jane Anson", "context": "2022 vintage", "quote": null}, {"score": "91", "critic": "Robert Parker''s Wine Advocate", "context": "2022 vintage", "quote": "A rich, ripe, somewhat Napa-styled Saint-Estèphe."}, {"score": "96", "critic": "Vinous", "context": "2020 vintage", "quote": "Represents the essence of classicism in Bordeaux."}, {"score": "95", "critic": "Wine Enthusiast", "context": "2020 vintage", "quote": "Richly structured, powered by dark tannins and rich blackberry fruits."}, {"score": "94", "critic": "Decanter", "context": "2020 vintage", "quote": "Pleasingly silky, polished and smooth. Sheer pleasure!"}, {"score": "93", "critic": "Jeb Dunnuck", "context": "2020 vintage", "quote": null}, {"score": "90", "critic": "Wine Spectator", "context": "2020 vintage", "quote": "Plump and open, with a burst of loganberry and mulberry fruit."}]}'::jsonb),
  ('c7e0f2de-8fd6-5cf7-b659-2a4d4253709b', '233c5174-3327-56ca-ab83-15b3a88ec490', NULL, 'needs_review', '31c483b5-ee62-505a-a6e2-f40c8f02e5ee', 'no', 'OU; Rabbi Its’hak Katz Kehal Yereim Paris Chareidi', 'AOC', 'Balanced fruit and structure giving it a soft finish with plenty of fresh blue and black fruit.', 'Perfect with rack of lamb in a red currant sauce or beef tenderloin with mushroom duxelle.', false, '{"source": "mm_website", "website_slug": "chateau-leydet-valentin", "name": "Chateau Leydet-Valentin", "producer": "Château Leydet-Valentin", "country": "France", "region": "Bordeaux", "appellation": "AOC", "grapes": "100% Merlot", "color": "Red", "mevushal": "No", "supervision": "OU; Rabbi Its’hak Katz Kehal Yereim Paris Chareidi", "pairing": "Perfect with rack of lamb in a red currant sauce or beef tenderloin with mushroom duxelle.", "score": "", "img": "/images/images/chateau-leydet-valentin.jpg?v=3", "new": false, "vintages": null, "tasting_note": "Balanced fruit and structure giving it a soft finish with plenty of fresh blue and black fruit.", "expert_note": "\"An elegant wine, this is ripe and also powerful. Some bitter chocolate flavors suggest heavy extraction, masking the ripe black fruits. It could well still soften, so best to leave this wine until 2021..\"- Roger Voss", "serve": "at 17 to 18°C (63 to 65°F).", "region_text": "Saint-Estèphe is one of the many famous Left Bank red wine appellations of Bordeaux, known for reds based on Cabernet Sauvignon and Merlot. Situated at the northern end of the Haut-Médoc region on the gravelly western shores of the Gironde estuary, Saint-Estèphe is separated from its famous neighbor, Pauillac, only by a stream, yet there are significant differences between them. With 1,229 hectares (3036 acres) it accounts for 8 percent of the vineyard area of the Médoc. Because Saint-Estèphe is marginally further from the gravel-bearing waters of the Garonne river, the soil here is far less stony than that found in the southern part of Haut-Médoc. Instead, a heavy clay and limestone base dominates this area, resulting in poorer-draining soils, delayed ripening and higher acidity levels in the wines.", "grape_text": "Merlot is a red wine grape variety with strong historic ties to Bordeaux and the southwest of France. Currently the the most searched-for wine on our database that is made from the grape is Petrus, from Pomerol. It is the predominant variety in most wines from Saint-Émilion and Pomerol, the area in which the variety originated. Merlot is now widely planted in wine regions across the world and, in terms of the volumes of wine produced internationally, it is rivaled only by its Bordeaux companion, Cabernet Sauvignon. Its characteristically reliable ripening is a main factor behind its increased presence over recent decades in the Médoc and Entre-Deux-Mers (where it has mostly replaced white varieties) areas of Bordeaux.", "critical_acclaim": []}'::jsonb),
  ('6f3d64da-3aeb-5b86-87c2-a38bf560c720', '6138d90a-7bde-52b3-9132-209e232e3bb2', NULL, 'needs_review', 'def501b0-5c36-506b-9882-100007be9011', 'no', 'R’ Its’hak Katz Kehal Yereim Paris Chareidi', 'AOC', 'Colour : Clear and bright with a light pink hue. Nose : Fine and delicate, white flowers and citrus . Palate : Delicate on notes of citrus and white fruits, an aromatic persistence out of the ordinary.', 'Enjoy with rich fish, vegetarian dishes, risotto and poultry', false, '{"source": "mm_website", "website_slug": "chateau-sainte-marguerite-fantastique-ros", "name": "Chateau Sainte Marguerite Fantastique Rosé", "producer": "Château Sainte Marguerite", "country": "France", "region": "Côtes de Provence", "appellation": "AOC", "grapes": "", "color": "Rosé", "mevushal": "No", "supervision": "R’ Its’hak Katz Kehal Yereim Paris Chareidi", "pairing": "Enjoy with rich fish, vegetarian dishes, risotto and poultry", "score": "", "img": "/images/images/chateau-sainte-marguerite-fantastique-ros-.jpg?v=4", "new": false, "vintages": null, "tasting_note": "Colour : Clear and bright with a light pink hue. Nose : Fine and delicate, white flowers and citrus . Palate : Delicate on notes of citrus and white fruits, an aromatic persistence out of the ordinary.", "expert_note": "“This is the top wine from the Jean-Pierre Fayard family Provence cru classé estate. It is full of ripe red fruits supported by a mineral texture. The wine is generous, bone dry but packed with great fruitiness and finished with refreshing acidity. This sophisticated wine could do with a few more months.” -ROGER VOSS", "serve": "chilled, 8 to 10°C (46 to 50°F).", "region_text": "Côtes de Provence AOC is the largest appellation of the Provence wine region in south-eastern France. It covers roughly 20,000 hectares (50,000 acres) of vineyards, which produce the vast majority of Provence''s rosé wine. This appellation includes most of the viticulture in the Var department – essentially the eastern half of the Provence wine region – apart from 2250 hectares (5500 acres) due north of Toulon which is set aside for the Côteaux Varois en Provence appellation. Although it also covers red and white wine, about 80 percent of Côtes de Provence''s output is rosé. This is made predominantly from Grenache, Syrah, Mourvèdre, Cinsaut grape varieties plus the quintessentially Provencal red grape Tibouren.", "grape_text": "Cinsaut – Grenache blends are made up of two important grape varieties from southern France, and are vinified as either red or rosé wines. The two varieties have much in common; both Grenache and Cinsaut are lighter bodied than other Rhone varieties, have strong resistance to droughts, and perform best when overcropping is avoided. Grenache is of particular importance in the south of France. It is the predominant variety in the prestigious wines of Chateauneuf-du-Pape, and is used in myriad appellations all along the Mediterranean coast. Cinsaut is also permitted in many appellations, but its main function is as a blending variety – while Grenache has sufficient character to be made into a wine on its own, Cinsaut rarely does.", "critical_acclaim": []}'::jsonb),
  ('798085d5-e548-5a2e-88dd-5fe07de216de', 'd14adc67-904b-5ae3-8a4b-f2da579a3e4c', NULL, 'needs_review', 'def501b0-5c36-506b-9882-100007be9011', 'no', 'R’ Its’hak Katz Kehal Yereim Paris Chareidi', 'AOC', 'The appearance, very light pink, is clear and bright. Floral and delicate nose of white flowers and citrus. It has a finely acidulous mouth, with notes of peach, citrus peel and exotic fruit.', 'Enjoy with truffle risotto, sushi and thai dishes.', false, '{"source": "mm_website", "website_slug": "chateau-sainte-marguerite-ros", "name": "Chateau Sainte Marguerite Rosé", "producer": "Château Sainte Marguerite", "country": "France", "region": "Côtes de Provence", "appellation": "AOC", "grapes": "40% Grenache 40% Cinsault 20% Syrah", "color": "Rosé", "mevushal": "No", "supervision": "R’ Its’hak Katz Kehal Yereim Paris Chareidi", "pairing": "Enjoy with truffle risotto, sushi and thai dishes.", "score": "", "img": "/images/images/chateau-sainte-marguerite-ros-.jpg?v=4", "new": false, "vintages": null, "tasting_note": "The appearance, very light pink, is clear and bright. Floral and delicate nose of white flowers and citrus. It has a finely acidulous mouth, with notes of peach, citrus peel and exotic fruit.", "expert_note": "“Super-pale – far more so than the standard Cuvee of Ste Marguerite. Delicate but also persistent. Brilliant! Made from old-vine Grenache and cinsault that dates back to 1936.”-Victoria More", "serve": "chilled, 8 to 10°C (46 to 50°F).", "region_text": "Côtes de Provence AOC is the largest appellation of the Provence wine region in south-eastern France. It covers roughly 20,000 hectares (50,000 acres) of vineyards, which produce the vast majority of Provence''s rosé wine. This appellation includes most of the viticulture in the Var department – essentially the eastern half of the Provence wine region – apart from 2250 hectares (5500 acres) due north of Toulon which is set aside for the Côteaux Varois en Provence appellation. Although it also covers red and white wine, about 80 percent of Côtes de Provence''s output is rosé. This is made predominantly from Grenache, Syrah, Mourvèdre, Cinsaut grape varieties plus the quintessentially Provencal red grape Tibouren.", "grape_text": "Cinsaut – Grenache blends are made up of two important grape varieties from southern France, and are vinified as either red or rosé wines. The two varieties have much in common; both Grenache and Cinsaut are lighter bodied than other Rhone varieties, have strong resistance to droughts, and perform best when overcropping is avoided. Grenache is of particular importance in the south of France. It is the predominant variety in the prestigious wines of Chateauneuf-du-Pape, and is used in myriad appellations all along the Mediterranean coast. Cinsaut is also permitted in many appellations, but its main function is as a blending variety – while Grenache has sufficient character to be made into a wine on its own, Cinsaut rarely does.", "critical_acclaim": []}'::jsonb),
  ('bc2ef00b-ae6b-53d2-a534-0f14bf0467ed', 'b5c3177d-5448-59e6-b056-0120bafe8a8f', '2022', 'needs_review', '47f551ff-b79d-5a61-bd1e-c3063e39686c', 'no', 'OU; Rabbi Its’hak Katz Kehal Yereim Paris Chareidi', 'Grand Cru Classé', 'Dark purple with cassis and black fruit on the nose. Full bodied, deeply extracted with classic velvety texture only Smit Haut wines can resemble.', 'Ideal with classic meat dishes, veal, beef, lamb, duck, game, roast chicken, roasted, braised and grilled dishes.', false, '{"source": "mm_website", "website_slug": "chateau-smith-haut-lafitte", "name": "Chateau Smith Haut Lafitte", "producer": "Château Smith Haut Lafitte", "country": "France", "region": "Bordeaux", "appellation": "Pessac-Léognan Grand Cru Classé", "grapes": "64% Cabernet Sauvignon, 32% Merlot, 3% Cabernet Franc, 1% Petit Verdot (2022)", "color": "Red", "mevushal": "No", "supervision": "OU; Rabbi Its’hak Katz Kehal Yereim Paris Chareidi", "pairing": "Ideal with classic meat dishes, veal, beef, lamb, duck, game, roast chicken, roasted, braised and grilled dishes.", "score": "100 WA", "img": "/images/images/chateau-smith-haut-lafitte.jpg?v=3", "new": false, "vintages": "2022, 2019, 2014, 2009", "tasting_note": "Dark purple with cassis and black fruit on the nose. Full bodied, deeply extracted with classic velvety texture only Smit Haut wines can resemble.", "expert_note": null, "serve": "at 17 to 18°C (63 to 65°F). Decant young vintages for an hour.", "region_text": "Pessac-Léognan is a prestigious appellation for red wine in the Bordeaux region of south-western France. It was carved out of the Graves sub-region in 1987 as recognition for its high quality red and white wines. Many of the estates in what is now Pessac-Léognan were the best performers in the Graves Classification of 1959. The regions wines tend to be based on the Cabernet Sauvignon and Cabernet Franc grape varieties. They best suit the terroir of Pessac-Léognan. The dominant soil type is the same gravel (and sand) which gave Graves its name. The red grape varieties of the appellation covers approximately 1491 hectares (3684 acres).", "grape_text": "Cabernet Sauvignon – Merlot wines are made from two of the world''s most famous and most widely grown wine grapes. The pair form the foundation of many of the great wines of Bordeaux, where this classic blend (often dubbed \"Bordeaux Blend\") is thought to have originated. For centuries, Cabernet Sauvignon and Merlot have been the quintessential Bordeaux wine grapes, but their fame and popularity have now taken them far beyond the banks of the Garonne, Dordogne and Gironde, to the furthest reaches of the wine world. In California the blend is often labeled as Meritage – providing the producer meets the requirements of the Meritage Alliance. The Australian regions of Coonawarra, Margaret River and Yarra Valley are highly regarded for their unique expressions of the blend. South Africa''s Stellenbosch region also produces some earthy and savory examples that defy many of the commonly held perceptions about New World wine. In other New World countries the blend is often abbreviated to Cabernet Merlot, although this mix could include Cabernet Franc as well.", "critical_acclaim": [{"score": "100", "critic": "Jeb Dunnuck", "context": "2022 vintage", "quote": "One of the greatest wines from the estate."}, {"score": "100", "critic": "Decanter", "context": "2022 vintage", "quote": null}, {"score": "98", "critic": "James Suckling", "context": "2022 vintage", "quote": "The polish, texture, complexity and patina are very impressive."}, {"score": "97+", "critic": "Vinous", "context": "2022 vintage", "quote": "Silky, elegant and nuanced. A wine of precision and class."}, {"score": "96+", "critic": "Robert Parker''s Wine Advocate", "context": "2022 vintage", "quote": "Needs time to digest its élevage."}, {"score": "95", "critic": "Wine Spectator", "context": "2022 vintage", "quote": "A warm gush of cassis, plum purée and cherry preserve flavors."}