uch for its beautiful buildings and scenery as for its wine. Its steep, narrow, cobbled streets, overlooked by its Romanesque church and the iconic 13th-century Tour du Roy tower are a reminder of the town''s long history.", "grape_text": "The Merlot-Cabernet Franc duet is an established and important variant on the classic Bordeaux blend, particularly on the Right Bank. It is used in the prestigious and Saint-Émilion and Pomerol appellations, and is behind some very high-profile wines. Merlot is usually used in higher proportions in this blend, thanks (in part) to its broad appeal and higher profile than Cabernet Franc. It provides most of the fruit component, offering up flavors of mulberries, plum and dark berries.", "critical_acclaim": [{"score": "98", "critic": "Vinous", "context": "2020 vintage", "quote": "A stunner. Rich, deep and explosive."}, {"score": "95 to 97", "critic": "Robert Parker''s Wine Advocate", "context": "2020, barrel sample", "quote": "Energetic, crunchy black fruits with a lively backbone."}]}'::jsonb),
  ('dd36f9c5-7bd0-59d6-b3cc-b2730d356e2d', '29dc3d29-3064-5bee-ac15-c25d55ad9567', NULL, 'needs_review', '31c483b5-ee62-505a-a6e2-f40c8f02e5ee', 'no', 'OU; Rabbi Its’hak Katz Kehal Yereim Paris Chareidi', 'AOC', 'Deep purple in color with red cherries, ripe bramble and pipe tobacco. On palate silky texture medium to full body with layers of ripe crushed berries, cassis and a touch of earthy materials.', 'Ideal Pairing Roast chicken, potato gratin, rib eye steak.', false, '{"source": "mm_website", "website_slug": "chateau-valandraud-virginie-de-valandraud", "name": "Chateau Valandraud Virginie de Valandraud", "producer": "Château Valandraud", "country": "France", "region": "Bordeaux", "appellation": "AOC", "grapes": "100% Merlot", "color": "Red", "mevushal": "No", "supervision": "OU; Rabbi Its’hak Katz Kehal Yereim Paris Chareidi", "pairing": "Ideal Pairing Roast chicken, potato gratin, rib eye steak.", "score": "", "img": "/images/images/chateau-valandraud-virginie-de-valandraud.jpg?v=3", "new": false, "vintages": null, "tasting_note": "Deep purple in color with red cherries, ripe bramble and pipe tobacco. On palate silky texture medium to full body with layers of ripe crushed berries, cassis and a touch of earthy materials.", "expert_note": "\"Barrel Sample. This beautiful wine, full of great fruit and balanced dusty tannins. It is ripe and stylish, with all the elements in place. it should mature well.\" -Wine Enthusiast", "serve": "at 17 to 18°C (63 to 65°F).", "region_text": "Saint-Émilion is an appellation and key wine town in the Libournais district of Bordeaux, important in terms of both quality and quantity. The most searched-for Saint-Émilion wine on our database is Château Cheval Blanc. The town lies just a few miles north of the Dordogne, in the final stages of the river''s journey from the hills of the Massif Central to the Gironde estuary. It is renowned as much for its beautiful buildings and scenery as for its wine. Its steep, narrow, cobbled streets, overlooked by its Romanesque church and the iconic 13th-century Tour du Roy tower are a reminder of the town''s long history.", "grape_text": "The Merlot-Cabernet Franc duet is an established and important varMerlot is a red wine grape variety with strong historic ties to Bordeaux and the southwest of France. Currently the the most searched-for wine on our database that is made from the grape is Petrus, from Pomerol. It is the predominant variety in most wines from Saint-Émilion and Pomerol, the area in which the variety originated. Merlot is now widely planted in wine regions across the world and, in terms of the volumes of wine produced internationally, it is rivaled only by its Bordeaux companion, Cabernet Sauvignon. Its characteristically reliable ripening is a main factor behind its increased presence over recent decades in the Médoc and Entre-Deux-Mers (where it has mostly replaced white varieties) areas of Bordeaux.", "critical_acclaim": []}'::jsonb),
  ('8dde558c-7167-5400-9fb7-d641b449c89a', 'a5d38246-b026-565a-9bc7-d9c4bfb4a867', NULL, 'needs_review', '9dc9da91-b568-5f83-9177-2ff88b0e1053', 'no', 'R’ Its’hak Katz Kehal Yereim Paris Chareidi', NULL, 'A juicy palate of fleshy, white fruit (such as Asian pear) only underscores the striking aromas on this elegant Bordeaux Blanc. Generous tropical notes of kiwi & lychee mingle with honeyed floral tones. A fine, fuller texture aligns with precise acidity.', 'Foie gras is a perfect pairing. Can also be paired with roasted chicken & veal that are either spicy, or sweet.', false, '{"source": "mm_website", "website_slug": "clos-des-lunes-lune-dargent", "name": "Clos des Lunes Lune d''Argent", "producer": "Clos des Lunes", "country": "France", "region": "Bordeaux", "appellation": "Bordeaux Blanc", "grapes": "100% Sémillon", "color": "White", "mevushal": "No", "supervision": "R’ Its’hak Katz Kehal Yereim Paris Chareidi", "pairing": "Foie gras is a perfect pairing. Can also be paired with roasted chicken & veal that are either spicy, or sweet.", "score": "", "img": "/images/images/clos-des-lunes-lune-d-argent.jpg?v=3", "new": false, "vintages": null, "tasting_note": "A juicy palate of fleshy, white fruit (such as Asian pear) only underscores the striking aromas on this elegant Bordeaux Blanc. Generous tropical notes of kiwi & lychee mingle with honeyed floral tones. A fine, fuller texture aligns with precise acidity.", "expert_note": "“The nose has touches of fresh lemons and exotic fruits. The salinity of Lune d’ Argent is noticed thanks to the finish. This wine is a clever companionship between the concentration of white fruits flavors and refreshing minerality, a straight-forward wine” -Jeff Love", "serve": "lightly chilled, 10 to 13°C (50 to 55°F).", "region_text": "Côtes de Provence AOC is the largest appellation of the Provence wine region in south-eastern France. It covers roughly 20,000 hectares (50,000 acres) of vineyards, which produce the vast majority of Provence''s rosé wine. This appellation includes most of the viticulture in the Var department – essentially the eastern half of the Provence wine region – apart from 2250 hectares (5500 acres) due north of Toulon which is set aside for the Côteaux Varois en Provence appellation. Although it also covers red and white wine, about 80 percent of Côtes de Provence''s output is rosé. This is made predominantly from Grenache, Syrah, Mourvèdre, Cinsaut grape varieties plus the quintessentially Provencal red grape Tibouren.", "grape_text": "Sémillon is one of the wine world''s unsung heroes. The gold-skinned grape produces France''s most famous and revered sweet wines, notably Sauternes, and some of the greatest dry white wines of Australia (specifically those of the Hunter Valley). And yet, few Sémillons between these two extremes attract much attention. The thick-skinned grape is characterized by its autumnal colors in the vineyard. Sémillon is vigorous and easy to cultivate, and buds later (but ripens earlier) than its most common blending partner, Sauvignon Blanc. Although the fruit is usually bright golden-green, it is not uncommon to find pink- and copper-colored berries around harvest time. Certainly, when the grapes are affected by the noble rot, Botrytis cinerea, they take on darker hues and gnarled textures; viticulturists view the sight with anticipation and excitement.", "critical_acclaim": []}'::jsonb),
  ('35292fbd-5b63-5e1d-b231-ac863150aac7', '7e765545-7d06-5e48-be6c-a9fc92c4fc00', NULL, 'needs_review', '2a81a8d5-8b39-5c95-be88-1b0115fa6cc8', 'no', 'OU; IKUI; Beit Yosef Chareidi', 'DOC', 'The wine is bright red with a fragrant and aromatic bouquet of red fruit, minerals and flowers. The wine has a cheery and red berry character with notes of balsamic, cedar and earth. Full bodied with powerful structure and balanced tannins.', 'Enjoy with beef, lamb, veal poultry and cured meats', false, '{"source": "mm_website", "website_slug": "fabio-tassi-aqua-bona-rosso", "name": "Fabio Tassi Aqua Bona Rosso", "producer": "Fabio Tassi", "country": "Italy", "region": "Tuscany", "appellation": "DOC", "grapes": "100% Sangiovese", "color": "Red", "mevushal": "No", "supervision": "OU; IKUI; Beit Yosef Chareidi", "pairing": "Enjoy with beef, lamb, veal poultry and cured meats", "score": "", "img": "/images/images/fabio-tassi-aqua-bona-rosso.jpg?v=3", "new": false, "vintages": null, "tasting_note": "The wine is bright red with a fragrant and aromatic bouquet of red fruit, minerals and flowers. The wine has a cheery and red berry character with notes of balsamic, cedar and earth. Full bodied with powerful structure and balanced tannins.", "expert_note": "Franci Franca winery, run by his son Fabio Tassi, is strongly bonded with Montalcino’s territory since its origin. Its wine clearly expresses its tie to the land with elegance and uniqueness. The Bettina cuvee was made in Honor of Betty Sitt by her husband and Children.", "serve": "at 16 to 17°C (61 to 63°F).", "region_text": "The scenic hills of Tuscany are home to the cities of Florence and Siena, as well as to Chianti, a blend made primarily from the Sangiovese grape. It was once known as an inexpensive table wine marked by its bulbous bottle and woven base, but efforts by innovative winemakers have produced very fine examples that have made the wine world reconsider the cliché. Chianti is a dry, medium-bodied wine with high acids, moderate tannins and flavors of cherry, herbs and sweet spice. One of the most aged and revered wines in Italy is Brunello di Montalcino, made entirely from a clone of Sangiovese grown near the town of Montalcino. It is a medium- to full-bodied dry wine that tastes of black fruits, earth and pepper.", "grape_text": "Sangiovese (or Nielluccio in Corsica), a dark-berried vine, is the most widely planted grape variety in Italy. Virtually synonymous with the red wines of Tuscany, and all the romanticism that goes with the territory, Sangiovese is the core constituent in some of the great names in Italian wine. Italy''s love affair with Sangiovese – and indeed the world''s – is generations old, though recent grapevine research suggests the variety is not as ancient as once thought.", "critical_acclaim": []}'::jsonb),
  ('eca9c9c9-b90e-5045-bbc2-777c07b3cdc2', '89217fae-da5d-528f-8244-40f95a703eae', NULL, 'needs_review', '2a81a8d5-8b39-5c95-be88-1b0115fa6cc8', 'no', 'OU; IKUI; Beit Yosef Chareidi', 'DOCG', 'The wine is bright red with a fragrant and aromatic bouquet of red fruit, minerals and flowers. The wine has a cheery and red berry character with notes of balsamic, cedar and earth. Full bodied with powerful structure and balanced tannins.', 'Pair with rosemary lamb chops or a dinner of roast duck.', false, '{"source": "mm_website", "website_slug": "fabio-tassi-brunello-di-montalcino", "name": "Fabio Tassi Brunello di Montalcino", "producer": "Fabio Tassi", "country": "Italy", "region": "Tuscany", "appellation": "DOCG", "grapes": "100% Sangiovese", "color": "Red", "mevushal": "No", "supervision": "OU; IKUI; Beit Yosef Chareidi", "pairing": "Pair with rosemary lamb chops or a dinner of roast duck.", "score": "", "img": "/images/images/fabio-tassi-brunello-di-montalcino.jpg?v=3", "new": false, "vintages": null, "tasting_note": "The wine is bright red with a fragrant and aromatic bouquet of red fruit, minerals and flowers. The wine has a cheery and red berry character with notes of balsamic, cedar and earth. Full bodied with powerful structure and balanced tannins.", "expert_note": "Franci Franca winery, run by his son Fabio Tassi, is strongly bonded with Montalcino’s territory since its origin. Its wine clearly expresses its tie to the land with elegance and uniqueness. The Bettina cuvee was made in Honor of Betty Sitt by her husband and Children.", "serve": "at 16 to 17°C (61 to 63°F).", "region_text": "The scenic hills of Tuscany are home to the cities of Florence and Siena, as well as to Chianti, a blend made primarily from the Sangiovese grape. It was once known as an inexpensive table wine marked by its bulbous bottle and woven base, but efforts by innovative winemakers have produced very fine examples that have made the wine world reconsider the cliché. Chianti is a dry, medium-bodied wine with high acids, moderate tannins and flavors of cherry, herbs and sweet spice. One of the most aged and revered wines in Italy is Brunello di Montalcino, made entirely from a clone of Sangiovese grown near the town of Montalcino. It is a medium- to full-bodied dry wine that tastes of black fruits, earth and pepper.", "grape_text": "Sangiovese (or Nielluccio in Corsica), a dark-berried vine, is the most widely planted grape variety in Italy. Virtually synonymous with the red wines of Tuscany, and all the romanticism that goes with the territory, Sangiovese is the core constituent in some of the great names in Italian wine. Italy''s love affair with Sangiovese – and indeed the world''s – is generations old, though recent grapevine research suggests the variety is not as ancient as once thought.", "critical_acclaim": []}'::jsonb),
  ('883d6021-4220-5d4b-bf39-c64033312efe', 'c77657b4-53c2-54f8-ba66-8bed82ab198d', NULL, 'needs_review', '1b401aee-3668-555b-b749-176506f9388b', 'no', 'OU; IKU; Beit Yosef Chareidi', 'IGT', 'Medium gold in color, aromas of tropical fruits & sweet corn complement undertones of fresh herbs & vanilla. On the palate, it is rich and full-bodied with good acidity & a creamy texture. There are ripe apples, buttery toast, lime peel & toasted nut flavors with some vanilla.', 'Pair this wine with hearty risottos, béchamel sauces, roasted game, and baba ghanoush.', false, '{"source": "mm_website", "website_slug": "falesco-ferentano", "name": "Falesco Ferentano", "producer": "Falesco", "country": "Italy", "region": "Lazio", "appellation": "Lazio IGT", "grapes": "100% Roscetto", "color": "White", "mevushal": "No", "supervision": "OU; IKU; Beit Yosef Chareidi", "pairing": "Pair this wine with hearty risottos, béchamel sauces, roasted game, and baba ghanoush.", "score": "", "img": "/images/images/falesco-ferentano.jpg?v=3", "new": false, "vintages": null, "tasting_note": "Medium gold in color, aromas of tropical fruits & sweet corn complement undertones of fresh herbs & vanilla. On the palate, it is rich and full-bodied with good acidity & a creamy texture. There are ripe apples, buttery toast, lime peel & toasted nut flavors with some vanilla.", "expert_note": "Cotarella is a winery and vineyard established in Montefiascone, Italy in 1979. Cotarella has been described as a \"state-of-the-art winery\" and its production facilities are now located in Montecchio. Described as a \"sprawling property\" 370 acres of vineyards. Annual production is almost 3 million bottles. The estate is on the border of Lazio and Umbria.", "serve": "chilled, 8 to 10°C (46 to 50°F).", "region_text": "Lazio is a region in central Italy, and home to the ancient capital city of Rome. The region''s reputation is mainly based on its white wines, the mainstay grape varieties being Trebbiano, Malvasia di Candia and Malvasia Puntinata. Traditionally these wines were fat, rounded, abboccato and made for immediate consumption. Today the styles are lighter, drier and crisper thanks to modern vinification methods.", "grape_text": "Roscetto is an ancient white-wine variety grown in such minute quantities that today, only one producer in Italy''s Lazio region grows the variety, for use in Lazio IGT wines. It is entirely possible that the last remaining plantings of Roscetto vines are restricted to a six-hectare plot near Montefiascone, northern Lazio. The low-yielding Roscetto variety produces small, tightly clustered berries with a high concentration of sugar balanced by crisp acidity. However, because so few commercial wines are made with Roscetto, it''s difficult to make generalizations about the grape''s fruit character. Some blends are released as Est! Est!! Est!!! wine, in which Roscetto makes up usually 30 to 40 percent; Trebbiano dominates, followed by Malvasia. Varietal releases include a dry sparkling wine, a dry still wine, and a sweet passito wine made from dried grapes. No DOC exists for Roscetto when made in purezza (pure), so these wines are released under the generic Lazio IGT designation.", "critical_acclaim": []}'::jsonb),
  ('8ce208e8-4f48-5679-bfd0-baf337564d3b', '3787a514-3b11-518e-b331-ccdc795bc674', '2018', 'needs_review', 'de870e07-a53c-51ab-8679-f04ee782f7e8', 'no', 'R’ Its’hak Katz Kehal Yereim Paris Chareidi', 'IGT', 'Deep opaque purple in color, this delicious red aromas of cassis, herbs, tobacco, cedar, and slate, which continue to unfold on palate. Structurally, the wine has a perfect balance between the firm, fine tannins & elegant velvety mouth-feel. These factors coalesce to make a long-lived & full-bodied.', 'Pair this wine with grilled steak, demi-glaces, brisket, and Moroccan lamb tagines.', false, '{"source": "mm_website", "website_slug": "falesco-marciliano", "name": "Falesco Marciliano", "producer": "Falesco", "country": "Italy", "region": "Umbria", "appellation": "Umbria IGT", "grapes": "70% Cabernet Sauvignon, 30% Cabernet Franc", "color": "Red", "mevushal": "No", "supervision": "R’ Its’hak Katz Kehal Yereim Paris Chareidi", "pairing": "Pair this wine with grilled steak, demi-glaces, brisket, and Moroccan lamb tagines.", "score": "", "img": "/images/images/falesco-marciliano.jpg?v=3", "new": false, "vintages": "2018", "tasting_note": "Deep opaque purple in color, this delicious red aromas of cassis, herbs, tobacco, cedar, and slate, which continue to unfold on palate. Structurally, the wine has a perfect balance between the firm, fine tannins & elegant velvety mouth-feel. These factors coalesce to make a long-lived & full-bodied.", "expert_note": "Cotarella is a winery and vineyard established in Montefiascone, Italy in 1979. Cotarella has been described as a \"state-of-the-art winery\" and its production facilities are now located in Montecchio. Described as a \"sprawling property\" 370 acres of vineyards. Annual production is almost 3 million bottles. The estate is on the border of Lazio and Umbria.", "serve": "at 17 to 18°C (63 to 65°F).", "region_text": "Despite a reputation as the green heart of central Italy, Umbria remains terra incognita to most wine drinkers, overshadowed by its neighbor, Tuscany. However, the winds of change are blowing in Italy’s only central land-locked region. Orvieto, the major white wine of the region, has entered world markets and achieved visibility. A blend of Trebbiano, Verdello and other local grapes, it is dry to semi-dry, light- to medium-bodied and moderate in acidity. Orvietos have notes of citrus, minerals and apples, and are perfect for light pastas, poached fish or prosciutto.", "grape_text": "Cabernet Franc – Cabernet Sauvignon are two of the key grape varieties (along with Merlot) used in the red wines of Bordeaux. The combined blend of the two has been so successful that it has been adopted in wine regions the world over. Typically Cabernet Sauvignon is the dominant member in this blend, and provides both structure (acidic and tannic) and aromatic complexity (cassis, cedar, tobacco). The Cabernet Franc component brings a lifted, slightly more floral aroma, and a hint of spice on the palate. Exceptions to this rule of Cabernet Sauvignon dominance are most likely to be found in the Loire Valley, where Cabernet Franc has long been a staple red wine variety. In Tuscany this blend has been warmly adopted. Sassicaia – one of Italy''s most famous wines – is arguably one of the world''s finest examples of this marriage of the two Cabernet grapes, and is largely responsible for the proliferation of the style throughout the region. This \"Super Tuscan\" wine is routinely described as having characteristics of cassis and five-spice with firm tannins in its youth. With age these wines soften and start to show more secondary qualities – often led by Cabernet Franc – of tobacco, coffee and earthy minerals.", "critical_acclaim": []}'::jsonb),
  ('d674b3d3-d968-53cf-938b-c49918f5505c', '3e11dbd5-f953-5f1c-8137-798e9e80d605', '2018', 'needs_review', '1b401aee-3668-555b-b749-176506f9388b', 'no', 'R’ Its’hak Katz Kehal Yereim Paris Chareidi', 'IGT', 'Deep, ruby red color, a wide aromatic range of scents in which delicious vanilla notes, small red fruit, layers of jam and sweet spices combine. The taste appears to have a full aristocratic roundness and softness, typical of Merlot, with quite elegant, agreeable and lingering flavors.', 'Pairs brilliantly with cassoulet or hearty casseroles, smoked beef or cured sausages, and roasted lamb with mint sauce.', false, '{"source": "mm_website", "website_slug": "falesco-montiano", "name": "Falesco Montiano", "producer": "Falesco", "country": "Italy", "region": "Lazio", "appellation": "Lazio IGT", "grapes": "100% Merlot", "color": "Red", "mevushal": "No", "supervision": "R’ Its’hak Katz Kehal Yereim Paris Chareidi", "pairing": "Pairs brilliantly with cassoulet or hearty casseroles, smoked beef or cured sausages, and roasted lamb with mint sauce.", "score": "93 WA", "img": "/images/images/falesco-montiano.jpg?v=3", "new": false, "vintages": "2018", "tasting_note": "Deep, ruby red color, a wide aromatic range of scents in which delicious vanilla notes, small red fruit, layers of jam and sweet spices combine. The taste appears to have a full aristocratic roundness and softness, typical of Merlot, with quite elegant, agreeable and lingering flavors.", "expert_note": null, "serve": "at 17 to 18°C (63 to 65°F). Decant young vintages for an hour.", "region_text": "Lazio is a region in central Italy, and home to the ancient capital city of Rome. The region''s reputation is mainly based on its white wines, the mainstay grape varieties being Trebbiano, Malvasia di Candia and Malvasia Puntinata. Traditionally these wines were fat, rounded, abboccato and made for immediate consumption. Today the styles are lighter, drier and crisper thanks to modern vinification methods.", "grape_text": "Merlot is a red wine grape variety with strong historic ties to Bordeaux and the southwest of France. Currently the the most searched-for wine on our database that is made from the grape is Petrus, from Pomerol. It is the predominant variety in most wines from Saint-Émilion and Pomerol, the area in which the variety originated. Merlot is now widely planted in wine regions across the world and, in terms of the volumes of wine produced internationally, it is rivaled only by its Bordeaux companion, Cabernet Sauvignon. Its characteristically reliable ripening is a main factor behind its increased presence over recent decades in the Médoc and Entre-Deux-Mers (where it has mostly replaced white varieties) areas of Bordeaux.", "critical_acclaim": [{"score": "93", "critic": "Robert Parker''s Wine Advocate", "context": "2018 vintage", "quote": "A profound and deep personality with generous richness."}, {"score": "92", "critic": "James Suckling", "context": "2018 vintage", "quote": "Firm, creamy tannins frame a plush core of dark fruit."}, {"score": "92", "critic": "Vinous", "context": "2018 vintage", "quote": "Silky and enveloping yet superbly balanced."}]}'::jsonb),
  ('c1736017-adfa-5826-a20a-8a03f67f939a', 'e3fc1ec6-650b-57cc-b96b-9a9f824c565f', NULL, 'needs_review', 'dcc3e1dc-38b3-5cf2-a871-809218f7b6d5', 'no', 'R’ Its’hak Katz Kehal Yereim Paris Chareidi', NULL, 'The wine is a pale bright yellow, greenish tones, broad aromas of fine herbs. Very varied with notes of apple and pear. The palate is acidic, long and leaves a soft bitter finish that characterizes the variety.', 'Enjoy with lean fish, vegetarian dishes, veal and poultry.', false, '{"source": "mm_website", "website_slug": "hans-wirsching-dry-silvaner", "name": "Hans Wirsching Dry Silvaner", "producer": "Hans Wirsching", "country": "Germany", "region": "Franken", "appellation": "Franken", "grapes": "100% Silvaner", "color": "White", "mevushal": "No", "supervision": "R’ Its’hak Katz Kehal Yereim Paris Chareidi", "pairing": "Enjoy with lean fish, vegetarian dishes, veal and poultry.", "score": "", "img": "/images/images/hans-wirsching-dry-silvaner.jpg?v=3", "new": false, "vintages": null, "tasting_note": "The wine is a pale bright yellow, greenish tones, broad aromas of fine herbs. Very varied with notes of apple and pear. The palate is acidic, long and leaves a soft bitter finish that characterizes the variety.", "expert_note": "Its medium-sized, juicy grapes deliver a full-bodied, powerful wine with a neutral bouquet and a delicate, mild acidity, which is ideal for dry maturation.", "serve": "chilled, 8 to 10°C (46 to 50°F).", "region_text": "Franken, or Franconia in English, is a wine-growing region in the northwest of Germany''s historic state of Bavaria. Though Bavaria may be more famous for its beer, Franken boasts a proud viticultural tradition and is one of the most unique regions in the country. There are just over 6,100 hectares (15,073 ac) of vines planted in Franken and around 80 percent of these are white grape varieties. Here, Riesling plays second fiddle to the often overlooked Silvaner and Müller-Thurgau. Indeed, Silvaner lays claim as Franken''s leading grape variety and is one of the only places in the world where it outperforms Riesling.", "grape_text": "Silvaner is an underrated, neutral-scented, white-wine grape used widely in western Germany, and just across the Rhine in Alsace where it is spelled Sylvaner. Tiny quantities can also be found in Alto Adige, northern Italy, where it is a specialty of the Isarco Valley. One of the world''s less-revered wine grapes as its reputation falls far behind that of other Germanic varieties such as Riesling and Grüner Veltliner, Silvaner is something of a quiet achiever. It has its devotees in various countries outside of Germany including Romania, Slovakia, Croatia, Austria and the United States.", "critical_acclaim": []}'::jsonb),
  ('e407f3df-995b-5fd2-a2bc-4444f7b658ee', 'cb307eda-aa73-5014-9646-6832e4877446', NULL, 'needs_review', '78a8bd64-f5dc-5a06-8f60-f85f990a0f66', 'no', 'R’ Its’hak Katz Kehal Yereim Paris Chareidi', 'AOC', 'Very fine mousse and is delicate forming a steady stream of bubbles. A sandy yellow color with hint of straw. It is dominated by white fruit with distinguishing notes of tangy citrus yeast.', 'Enjoy with rich fish and mild and soft cheese', false, '{"source": "mm_website", "website_slug": "janisson-and-fils-grand-cru-brut", "name": "Janisson And Fils Grand Cru Brut", "producer": "Janisson & Fils", "country": "France", "region": "Champagne", "appellation": "AOC", "grapes": "90% Pinot Noir 10% Chardonnay", "color": "Sparkling", "mevushal": "No", "supervision": "R’ Its’hak Katz Kehal Yereim Paris Chareidi", "pairing": "Enjoy with rich fish and mild and soft cheese", "score": "", "img": "/images/images/janisson-fils-grand-cru-brut.jpg?v=4", "new": false, "vintages": null, "tasting_note": "Very fine mousse and is delicate forming a steady stream of bubbles. A sandy yellow color with hint of straw. It is dominated by white fruit with distinguishing notes of tangy citrus yeast.", "expert_note": "Savory aromatics of jambon cru and wet wool, with lovely sapidity on the palate. Linear yet with a certain richness", "serve": "well chilled, 6 to 8°C (43 to 46°F).", "region_text": "Champagne is the name of the world''s most famous sparkling wine, the appellation under which it is sold, and the French wine region it comes from. Currently the most searched-for example on our database is Dom Pérignon Brut. The term was widely used to refer to sparkling wines from all over the world. This has been a point of much controversy and legal wrangling in recent decades – Champagne is a legally controlled and restricted name.", "grape_text": "Pinot Noir is the dominant red wine grape of Burgundy, now adopted (and extensively studied) in wine regions all over the world. The variety''s elusive charm has carried it to all manner of vineyards. These extend from western Germany (as Spätburgunder) and northern Italy to Chile, South Africa, Australia, New Zealand and the USA. California, Oregon and New Zealand are arguably the greatest centers for the grape outside its home territory. However great Pinot Noir is made in all of these territories.", "critical_acclaim": []}'::jsonb),
  ('2ce88538-1aec-54f9-82a8-38d7abd9fe9a', 'a56123a2-935d-5181-9f70-c79a5b02f243', NULL, 'needs_review', '78a8bd64-f5dc-5a06-8f60-f85f990a0f66', 'no', 'R’ Its’hak Katz Kehal Yereim Paris Chareidi', 'AOC', 'The initial bouquet reveals wild strawberries, followed by wild berries, tart and vanilla. A distinct immediate mouth-feel directly followed sensations overwhelms the palate.', 'Enjoy with smoked salmon, duck, cold cuts and red fruits.', false, '{"source": "mm_website", "website_slug": "janisson-fils-brut-ros", "name": "Janisson And Fils Brut Rosé", "producer": "Janisson & Fils", "country": "France", "region": "Champagne", "appellation": "AOC", "grapes": "90% Pinot Noir 10% Chardonnay", "color": "Sparkling", "mevushal": "No", "supervision": "R’ Its’hak Katz Kehal Yereim Paris Chareidi", "pairing": "Enjoy with smoked salmon, duck, cold cuts and red fruits.", "score": "", "img": "/images/images/janisson-fils-brut-ros-.jpg?v=3", "new": false, "vintages": null, "tasting_note": "The initial bouquet reveals wild strawberries, followed by wild berries, tart and vanilla. A distinct immediate mouth-feel directly followed sensations overwhelms the palate.", "expert_note": "Savory aromatics of jambon cru and wet wool, with lovely sapidity on the palate. Linear yet with a certain richness", "serve": "well chilled, 6 to 8°C (43 to 46°F).", "region_text": "Champagne is the name of the world''s most famous sparkling wine, the appellation under which it is sold, and the French wine region it comes from. Currently the most searched-for example on our database is Dom Pérignon Brut. The term was widely used to refer to sparkling wines from all over the world. This has been a point of much controversy and legal wrangling in recent decades – Champagne is a legally controlled and restricted name.", "grape_text": "The term Champagne Blend refers to one of the world''s most distinctive wine styles – the sparkling wines made from Pinot Noir, Chardonnay and Pinot Meunier that are most famously associated with the Champagne region of northern France. The term, however, has come to evoke wines made in the methode traditionnelle around the world, and particularly in New World countries like the United States, Australia, New Zealand and South Africa. Pinot Noir and Chardonnay are the stars of the blend, usually used in roughly equal quantities in New World examples. The less glamorous Pinot Meunier really only comes into play in real, pure-blooded Champagne. In fact, there are seven permitted grape varieties in the Champagne AOC, although the remaining four – Pinot Gris, Pinot Blanc, Petit Meslier and Arbane – are so rarely used that they are typically forgotten, and are almost never used for sparkling wine production outside of Champagne (save for Pinot Blanc, which is used in Italy''s sparkling Franciacorta wines, and in Alsace).", "critical_acclaim": []}'::jsonb),
  ('8c8872b5-5994-571d-8191-be4f9e0feb7c', '3a46a4e1-7331-5aa8-9630-68785731a855', NULL, 'needs_review', 'abd6a2cd-88fc-5d39-bec2-78a6ab8ee761', 'no', 'OU; IKU; Beit Yosef Chareidi', 'DOC', 'An intense bouquet of grapefruit, pineapple, peach and fresh blossoms spoils our nose. The mouth feel is soft, fresh and pure. Nice balance and a hint of almond in the aftertaste.', 'Enjoy with herb-grilled or rotisserie chicken, light fish and pasta dishes, or mixed snack plates including cheeses, fruits, and nuts.', false, '{"source": "mm_website", "website_slug": "pescaja-arneis-terre-alfieri", "name": "Pescaja Arneis Terre Alfieri", "producer": "Pescaja", "country": "Italy", "region": "Piedmont", "appellation": "Terre Alfieri DOC", "grapes": "100% Arneis", "color": "White", "mevushal": "No", "supervision": "OU; IKU; Beit Yosef Chareidi", "pairing": "Enjoy with herb-grilled or rotisserie chicken, light fish and pasta dishes, or mixed snack plates including cheeses, fruits, and nuts.", "score": "", "img": "/images/images/pescaja-arneis-terre-alfieri.jpg?v=3", "new": false, "vintages": null, "tasting_note": "An intense bouquet of grapefruit, pineapple, peach and fresh blossoms spoils our nose. The mouth feel is soft, fresh and pure. Nice balance and a hint of almond in the aftertaste.", "expert_note": "The white wines made from 100% Arneis from the Colline Alfieri. -", "serve": "chilled, 8 to 10°C (46 to 50°F).", "region_text": "Cisterna d''Asti is a small DOC of the Piedmont wine region in the far northwest of Italy, created in 2002. Unlike the case with Barbera d''Asti DOCG or many other local DOCs, Cisterna is not a grape variety. This title covers red wines produced around the village of Cisterna d''Asti, and neigboring communes right in the centre of Piedmont. Cisterna d''Asti wine is made predominantly from Croatina, which must account for 80 percent of the blend. The balance may consist of other non-aromatic red varieties sanctioned under Piedmont''s wine laws. Grapes used to make wines sold under other local DOCs (Nebbiolo, Barbera and Dolcetto) are the obvious candidates.", "grape_text": "Arneis is a white wine grape variety from Italy''s much-respected Piedmont wine region. In a story shared by several renascent grape varieties (most obviously Viognier), Arneis has been rescued from the verge of extinction and is now enjoying something of a revival. By the 1960s, just a few hectares of Arneis vines remained, and only a handful of producers were making the wine. There are now more than 605 hectares (1500 acres) of Arneis vines in Piedmont. It produces floral-scented white wines, whose delicate aromas belie the wines'' relatively full bodies and generous flavors – typically of pear and apricot rounded out with a creamy hint of hazelnut.", "critical_acclaim": []}'::jsonb),
  ('20b44ff7-0147-5517-8d6a-cdf1fe8593cb', '2884018a-2f61-51c8-8365-0204752d3552', NULL, 'needs_review', 'abd6a2cd-88fc-5d39-bec2-78a6ab8ee761', 'no', 'OU; IKU; Beit Yosef Chareidi', 'DOC', 'Nebbiolo shows a very nice ruby ​​red color. Nice and fresh and fruity on the nose with delicious aromas of red fruit. We taste ripe cherries, fine acidity and light tannins. Very pleasant and soft to drink.', 'Meats, Braised Meats and Cheeses.', false, '{"source": "mm_website", "website_slug": "pescaja-tuk-terre-alfieri", "name": "Pescaja Tuké Terre Alfieri", "producer": "Pescaja", "country": "Italy", "region": "Piedmont", "appellation": "Terre Alfieri DOC", "grapes": "100% Nebbiolo", "color": "Red", "mevushal": "No", "supervision": "OU; IKU; Beit Yosef Chareidi", "pairing": "Meats, Braised Meats and Cheeses.", "score": "", "img": "/images/images/pescaja-tuk-terre-alfieri.jpg?v=3", "new": false, "vintages": null, "tasting_note": "Nebbiolo shows a very nice ruby ​​red color. Nice and fresh and fruity on the nose with delicious aromas of red fruit. We taste ripe cherries, fine acidity and light tannins. Very pleasant and soft to drink.", "expert_note": "Passion and craftsmanship are the watchwords with which Beppe Pescaja manages his oenological creature. Sun, heart and soul, the backbone of values that make up the poetic business plan, are combined excellently with a high level of technology in the cellar, which produces a range of territorial and genuine wines also precise and impeccable.", "serve": "at 17 to 18°C (63 to 65°F).", "region_text": "Cisterna d''Asti is a small DOC of the Piedmont wine region in the far northwest of Italy, created in 2002. Unlike the case with Barbera d''Asti DOCG or many other local DOCs, Cisterna is not a grape variety. This title covers red wines produced around the village of Cisterna d''Asti, and neigboring communes right in the centre of Piedmont. Cisterna d''Asti wine is made predominantly from Croatina, which must account for 80 percent of the blend. The balance may consist of other non-aromatic red varieties sanctioned under Piedmont''s wine laws. Grapes used to make wines sold under other local DOCs (Nebbiolo, Barbera and Dolcetto) are the obvious candidates.", "grape_text": "Nebnebiolo is the grape variety behind the top-quality red wines of Piedmont, northwestern Italy, the most notable of which are Barolo and Barbaresco. The most searched-for Nebbiolo wine on our database is currently Giacomo Conterno Monfortino Barolo Riserva. Nebbiolo wines are distinguished by their strong tannins, high acidity and distinctive scent – often described as \"tar and roses\". A less obvious characteristic, visible only over time, is their tendency to lose color. Within just a few years of vintage, most Nebbiolo wines begin fading from deep, violet-tinged ruby to a beautiful brick orange.", "critical_acclaim": []}'::jsonb),
  ('67f873cb-be74-5b7a-8ba3-d96f2600ccd9', '59c52d7c-786e-5934-a6df-55e1dbabf60d', NULL, 'needs_review', '98ff022d-1961-5933-b8a5-32d1c2a3ee8c', 'no', 'OU; Rabbi Its’hak Katz Kehal Yereim Paris Chareidi', 'DOC', 'Grape that benefits from the autumn colds to develop a fragrance of aromas that are reflected in an elegant wine in appearance, of an intense ruby ​​red color with violet reflections, aromas of wild berries, a soft and rightly tannic flavor.', 'Washed-rind and Epoisses, Langres, or Soumaintrain. meats such as roast lamb, rib of beef, breast of duck or game.', false, '{"source": "mm_website", "website_slug": "san-paolo-irpinia-aglianico", "name": "San Paolo Irpinia Aglianico", "producer": "San Paolo", "country": "Italy", "region": "Campania", "appellation": "DOC", "grapes": "100% Aglianico", "color": "Red", "mevushal": "No", "supervision": "OU; Rabbi Its’hak Katz Kehal Yereim Paris Chareidi", "pairing": "Washed-rind and Epoisses, Langres, or Soumaintrain. meats such as roast lamb, rib of beef, breast of duck or game.", "score": "", "img": "/images/images/san-paolo-irpinia-aglianico.jpg?v=4", "new": false, "vintages": null, "tasting_note": "Grape that benefits from the autumn colds to develop a fragrance of aromas that are reflected in an elegant wine in appearance, of an intense ruby ​​red color with violet reflections, aromas of wild berries, a soft and rightly tannic flavor.", "expert_note": "“The wine has an intense red and violet reflection. This translates into a bold, big red wines with notes of cherry and red fruit and a dash of cinnamon. Overall, it is a delicious red based wine with silky-soft and perfectly rounded tannins and a long finish.” - Wine Spectator", "serve": "at 17 to 18°C (63 to 65°F).", "region_text": "The Campania wine region is a geographically complex area south of Rome, leading inland from the Amalfi Coast and the Bay of Naples towards Mount Vesuvius then beyond, rising to a plateau upon which the Irpinia sub-region is located at around 600m above sea level. Campania accounts for just 3.3% of Italy’s vineyards, with 29,000ha of vines planted, yet the region has an extraordinary history of winemaking. Ancient Greek settlers bought vines to Italy when they began populating the south of the country in the 8th century BC. The Romans later embraced this vinous culture, and it was Falernian – from Campania’s modern-day Falerno del Massico DOC – that was their most prized wine.", "grape_text": "TAglianico is a red wine grape variety native to southern Italy. It is known to produce full-bodied red wines that show musky berry flavors with firm tannins and good aging potential. Even when grown in hot climates, Aglianico is capable of retaining high levels of acidity, which makes it a particularly useful vine in the Mediterranean. Despite its comparatively high acidity, the variety is late-ripening and vigorous, with a tendancy to produce high volumes of fruit if not checked by viticultural practices.", "critical_acclaim": []}'::jsonb),
  ('7297622f-991f-52bc-a701-1eeaed010c9f', '4daf31d2-2e92-5a33-9d08-ad3bf222a305', NULL, 'needs_review', 'ff069c44-41b2-5478-b362-94d814050791', 'no', 'OK; Rabbi Don Yoel Levy', 'Kabinett', 'Taste: elegant fruit coupled with an intense minerality, a finesse wine with käutriger aromas and pure elegance', 'ideal for Japanese cuisine such as sashimi & other sushi variations, fantastic food companion for classic German and French cuisine.', false, '{"source": "mm_website", "website_slug": "von-hvel-oberemmeler-riesling", "name": "von Hövel Oberemmeler Riesling", "producer": "von Hövel", "country": "Germany", "region": "Mosel", "appellation": "Kabinett", "grapes": "100% Riesling", "color": "White", "mevushal": "No", "supervision": "OK; Rabbi Don Yoel Levy", "pairing": "ideal for Japanese cuisine such as sashimi & other sushi variations, fantastic food companion for classic German and French cuisine.", "score": "", "img": "/images/images/von-h-vel-oberemmeler-riesling.jpg?v=3", "new": false, "vintages": null, "tasting_note": "Taste: elegant fruit coupled with an intense minerality, a finesse wine with käutriger aromas and pure elegance", "expert_note": "The Saar winery von Hövel in Konz-Oberemmel is part of the Association of German Prädikatsweingüter & is now in the 7th generation. Winemaker Maximilian von Kunow, winner of the Wine Award “Newcomer of the Year 2016”, values ​​naturally grown grapes that are gently handled and pressed. The wines mature in the vaulted cellar, which is more than 1100 years old.", "serve": "chilled, 8 to 10°C (46 to 50°F).", "region_text": "The wines are distinguished by their mineral flavors, acidity and light body, in dry to sweet styles. Notable vineyards include Bernkasteler Doctor, Piesporter Goldtröpfchen, Wehlener Sonnenuhr and Scharzhofberger (in Wiltingen). Key white varieties are Riesling and Müller-Thurgau.", "grape_text": "Riesling is a light-skinned, aromatic grape of German origin which is – if the majority of top wine critics are to be believed – the world''s finest white wine grape variety. For many, the claim above may seem at odds with the sea of chaptalized, low-quality wine exported from Germany in the late 20th Century. In truth, very little of that infamous wine was Riesling at all, but instead higher-yielding grapes such as Müller-Thurgau and Silvaner), but the reputation has nonetheless stuck. Riesling has also been stereotyped as just a sweet grape, used only to make sticky wines. But while botrytized Rieslings are among the finest sweet wines in the world, the majority of global Riesling wines are either dry or off-dry.", "critical_acclaim": []}'::jsonb),
